Description: Import a Rekordbox hot cue's saved loop, not just its position
 A Rekordbox hot cue can be a saved LOOP (set with the loop in/out controls
 then saved to a pad), not just a plain position - the ANLZ cue entry has a
 CUE_ENTRY_TYPE_LOOP variant with its own loop_time(), exactly like the
 anonymous "memory cue" loops that rekordboxfeature.cpp already handles
 correctly a few lines above this fix.
 .
 The hot-cue branch of both cue-parsing loops (the plain SECTION_TAGS_CUES
 format and the "extended", comment/colour-carrying SECTION_TAGS_CUES_2
 format) ignored this: it always passed mixxx::audio::kInvalidFramePos as
 the end position to setHotCue(), regardless of the entry's actual type,
 silently discarding the loop length and importing every such hot cue as a
 plain point. setHotCue() itself already does the right thing with a valid
 end position (CueType::Loop instead of CueType::HotCue) - it was simply
 never being given one for hot cues. Both branches now check the entry's
 type first and compute the real end position from loop_time() when it is a
 loop, the same way the memory-cue loop case already does.
Author: GRV6 build (local)
Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/library/rekordbox/rekordboxfeature.cpp b/src/library/rekordbox/rekordboxfeature.cpp
--- a/src/library/rekordbox/rekordboxfeature.cpp
+++ b/src/library/rekordbox/rekordboxfeature.cpp
@@ -1197,10 +1197,26 @@
                     if (hotCueIndex > lastHotCueIndex) {
                         lastHotCueIndex = hotCueIndex;
                     }
+                    // GRV6: a hot cue can be a saved LOOP in rekordbox, not just a position -
+                    // it has its own loop_time() exactly like a memory-cue loop does (see the
+                    // CUE_ENTRY_TYPE_LOOP case above). Passing kInvalidFramePos unconditionally,
+                    // as stock Mixxx does here, always creates a plain position cue and silently
+                    // drops the loop length. setHotCue() already knows what to do with a valid
+                    // end position (CueType::Loop instead of CueType::HotCue) - it was just
+                    // never being given one for hot cues.
+                    mixxx::audio::FramePos hotCueEndPosition = mixxx::audio::kInvalidFramePos;
+                    if (cueEntry->type() == rekordbox_anlz_t::CUE_ENTRY_TYPE_LOOP) {
+                        int endTime = static_cast<int>(cueEntry->loop_time()) - timingOffset;
+                        if (endTime < 1) {
+                            endTime = 1;
+                        }
+                        hotCueEndPosition = mixxx::audio::FramePos(
+                                sampleRateKhz * static_cast<double>(endTime));
+                    }
                     setHotCue(
                             track,
                             position,
-                            mixxx::audio::kInvalidFramePos,
+                            hotCueEndPosition,
                             hotCueIndex,
                             QString(),
                             mixxx::RgbColor::nullopt());
